From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: server, win32u: after a domain user's session the display keys can still be rewritten

Wine makes a token's primary group the owner of what it creates. Since
0205 a domain account's primary group is its domain's Domain Users, so the
keys its session's display setup writes in HKLM (Enum\DISPLAY, the monitor
class) were owned by a group the greeter and local accounts do not hold.
Their display setup could not delete them, and win32u's reg_empty_key()
retried the undeletable key for ever: the greeter spun at full CPU after
the first domain user signed out and no one could sign in again.

- server: a domain account's token keeps this machine's Users group as its
  owner, as a local account's does; its primary group is still the
  domain's.
- win32u: reg_empty_key() stops at a key or value it cannot delete instead
  of retrying it.

--- a/server/token.c
+++ b/server/token.c
@@ -1492,6 +1492,21 @@
     if (!token) return NULL;
     assert( token->primary_group );
 
+    /* create_token() makes the primary group the owner of what the token
+     * creates, and for a local account that is this machine's Users group,
+     * which every account's token holds -- so the display keys one session
+     * rewrites in HKLM (Enum\DISPLAY, the video map) stay deletable by the
+     * next one. A domain account's primary group is its domain's Domain
+     * Users, which the greeter and local accounts do not hold: their display
+     * setup could then never empty those keys again. The owner stays the
+     * machine's Users group; the primary group is still the domain's. */
+    if (domain_count)
+    {
+        struct group *group;
+        LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( group, &token->groups, struct group, entry )
+            if (equal_sid( &group->sid, &domain_users_sid )) token->owner = &group->sid;
+    }
+
     if (!token_assign_label( token, is_admin ? &high_label_sid : &medium_label_sid ))
     {
         release_object( token );
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -754,13 +754,15 @@
     DWORD size;
     HKEY hkey = key_name ? reg_open_ascii_key( root, key_name ) : root;
 
+    /* A subkey that cannot be deleted (another user's, in a shared prefix)
+     * stays at index 0: stop instead of retrying it for ever. */
     while (!NtEnumerateKey( hkey, 0, KeyNodeInformation, key, sizeof(buffer), &size ))
-        reg_delete_tree( hkey, key->Name, key->NameLength );
+        if (!reg_delete_tree( hkey, key->Name, key->NameLength )) break;
 
     while (!NtEnumerateValueKey( hkey, 0, KeyValueFullInformation, value, sizeof(buffer), &size ))
     {
         UNICODE_STRING name = { value->NameLength, value->NameLength, value->Name };
-        NtDeleteValueKey( hkey, &name );
+        if (NtDeleteValueKey( hkey, &name )) break;
     }
 
     if (hkey != root) NtClose( hkey );
